        faqs=[('University Admissions','Can I study in Italy after completing my studies in Nepal?','Your eligibility depends on your qualification, subject and the programme’s current admission call. An advisor can help compare your background with the published requirements.'),('Scholarships','Are scholarships guaranteed?','No. Awards depend on the authority’s eligibility criteria, assessment, available funds and deadlines. We help you understand the process and prepare your application.'),('Visa','Does an admission letter guarantee a student visa?','No. Admission and pre-enrollment support your application, but the competent consular authority makes the visa decision.'),('Documents','Which documents should I prepare first?','Start by gathering your passport, transcripts and qualification certificates. Confirm translation, legalization and recognition requirements for your specific university and visa pathway.'),('Accommodation','Can you help me find accommodation?','We can guide you through residences, scholarship housing and private rental options. Availability and contracts must be confirmed with the provider.'),('Entrance Tests','Do all universities require an entrance test?','No single test applies to every programme. Check each course’s current call for the accepted test, interview or selection process.'),('Tuition Fees','How much will tuition cost?','Fees depend on the programme, institution and any applicable income assessment or reduction. Use the current official fee schedule.'),('Living Costs','How should I plan my monthly budget?','Include rent, utilities, groceries, transport, insurance and personal expenses, plus one-time arrival costs. Get current local quotations for your chosen city.'),('Student Life','Do I need to speak Italian?','Some programmes teach in English, but practical Italian is valuable for daily life. Check the programme’s specific language requirements.'),('Post-Arrival Services','Will I receive support after arriving?','Discuss your support plan before departure. We can guide you through accommodation check-in, university enrollment and the relevant settlement procedures.')]
